 ## Background
-Spherical Harmonics are a set of orthogonal functions defined on the sphere, commonly used in computer graphics for lighting and view-dependent shading [G]. The encoder implementation described here is derived from neural rendering pipelines, specifically HashNeRF-pytorch [S1, unofficial].
